            {
                "entry_id": "22bdcf78-f169-3585-8118-ae545ea5e851",
                "word": "Li-Fi",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b0675572-d19b-3f59-90cf-e79f202642b7",
                        "entry_id": "22bdcf78-f169-3585-8118-ae545ea5e851",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Technologie de communication sans fil basée sur l’utilisation de clignotements à haute fréquence de la lumière visible émise par des diodes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Couche physique",
                            "Couche liaison"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04b2faad-be84-4d2e-8d09-fffeea6fb75c",
                                "sense_id": "b0675572-d19b-3f59-90cf-e79f202642b7",
                                "text": "Après les Arbres à Vent, il a annoncé vendredi 11 septembre que six salles de l’édifice seraient dotées d’une connexion internet par Light Fidelity (Li-Fi), une technologie de communication basée sur l’éclairage."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3660f776-7081-4273-8d16-b4a67bc9f6b9",
                        "source_entry_id": "22bdcf78-f169-3585-8118-ae545ea5e851",
                        "source_sense_id": "b0675572-d19b-3f59-90cf-e79f202642b7",
                        "target_lang_word": "Li-Fi",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8a1aa865-b816-415d-902c-060084eaf1f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "22bdcf78-f169-3585-8118-ae545ea5e851",
                        "source_sense_id": "b0675572-d19b-3f59-90cf-e79f202642b7",
                        "target_lang_word": "Li-Fi",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Li-Fi",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08b10994-e97e-3dd9-a543-725b767ae429",
                                        "entry_id": "7c2fc07d-66da-3337-b60a-e49380b4bc39",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bidirectional, high-speed, networked wireless communication technology similar to Wi-Fi but using visible light instead of radio waves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5dbd698-66e4-4133-985a-ea31a599c518",
                                                "sense_id": "08b10994-e97e-3dd9-a543-725b767ae429",
                                                "text": "Since Li-Fi uses just the light, it can be used safely in aircrafts^([sic]) and hospitals that are prone to interference from radio waves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f37d4030-019a-4d2e-9c89-9f39e78581c4",
                                                "sense_id": "08b10994-e97e-3dd9-a543-725b767ae429",
                                                "text": "The beauty of Li-Fi is that it uses existing infrastructure, avoiding the need for thousands of radio masts, as the current spectrum requires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e820daa-9ac5-4628-b67a-630c0396f5f9",
                                                "sense_id": "08b10994-e97e-3dd9-a543-725b767ae429",
                                                "text": "The vision is that a Li-Fi wireless network would complement existing heterogeneous RF wireless networks, and would provide significant spectrum relief by allowing cellular and wireless fidelity (Wi-Fi) systems to off-load a significant portion of wireless data traffic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "04cf4107-6111-4062-bf15-9523817f6027",
                        "source_entry_id": "22bdcf78-f169-3585-8118-ae545ea5e851",
                        "source_sense_id": "b0675572-d19b-3f59-90cf-e79f202642b7",
